              "type": "text",
              "text": "Sam, Eddie and Maria invested $1500, $5000 and $9500 respectively when they started a new business. The total annual profit of $480 000 was shared in the same ratio as their investment. How much did each person receive?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p58-q1-answer",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sam: $45 000; Eddie: $150 000; Maria: $285 000.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "The investment ratio is $1500:5000:9500=3:10:19$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Total parts}&=3+10+19=32\\\\32\\text{ parts}&=\\$480\\,000\\\\1\\text{ part}&=\\$480\\,000\\div32=\\$15\\,000\\\\3\\text{ parts}&=3\\times\\$15\\,000=\\$45\\,000\\\\10\\text{ parts}&=10\\times\\$15\\,000=\\$150\\,000\\\\19\\text{ parts}&=19\\times\\$15\\,000=\\$285\\,000\\end{align*}$$\nSam receives \\$45 000, Eddie receives \\$150 000 and Maria receives \\$285 000.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
